{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Continuing the run: the previously reviewed store-failure finding is confirmed in scope, and this turn adds the direct check for the second accepted obligation. Submission is action=check on unit-claim-snapshot-install-stale-watermark, reusing the accepted binding bind-install-snapshot-watermark (Raft.installSnapshot, raft.go 1814-1955). draft/assurance_generated_test.go seeds a real InmemStore with entries 1..10 (watermark (10,1)) wrapped so IsMonotonic() is true, builds Raft with the internal skipStartup flag, starts only the real runFSM consumer so the handler's restore request can complete, and then drives a well-formed InstallSnapshotRequest with LastLogIndex=4, a genuine msgpack FSM payload and a voter configuration. Because the store is monotonic, installSnapshot takes removeOldLogs and clears the whole log while never calling setLastLog. draft/plan.json fixes prerequisites admit=install_request and store=store_after_install (install_succeeded=true), admission_alias=admit, identity 'node', and one event_assertion: under trigger install_succeeded==true the result event's raft_last_log_index must equal the correlated store prerequisite's snapshot_index. I compiled and ran this exact harness locally in the scratch copy draft/cc1 (not part of the submission): it builds, installSnapshot succeeds (resp.Success true), and the emitted observation is {\\\"raft_last_log_index\\\":10,\\\"raft_last_log_term\\\":1,\\\"raft_last_index\\\":10,\\\"snapshot_index\\\":4,\\\"store_last_index\\\":0,\\\"applied_index\\\":4} - the follower reports log index 10 while the install cleared the store (last index 0) and put the snapshot at 4, so the equality oracle (10 == 4) is expected to record a violation witness pending the checker_correspondence review. The applicability boundary is explicit: the ordinary catch-up path where the follower is strictly behind the snapshot is unaffected, and reachability of a legal leader history producing watermark-above-snapshot is stated as an open premise in the obligation and in the plan's uncertainties. Preflight validation returns valid with no diagnostics.\"}"}}
